From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Anthony Fu (via agent)" <reg-github-bot@antfu.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:34:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: sync the web app's host list through the daemon that
 serves it

Every browser that opened the web app had to add each host again, and a
host changed on one device stayed stale on the others.

The daemon now keeps the app's host list in app-host-registry.json, read
and saved with daemon.app_host_registry.get and .set, gated on
server_info.features.appHostRegistry. The daemon stores the list as an
opaque string with a revision and saves a write only when it was made
against the current revision.

The web app asks the page's own /api/status which daemon served it. While
that host is saved and connected, it polls the list every 5 seconds and
on every local change, merges both sides host by host against the list it
last agreed on, and saves the merge back. Adding, editing and removing a
host on one device reaches every other device. A device's first sync adds
its hosts to the list. A browser that has not saved the serving daemon
gets its address prefilled in Direct connection, so only the password is
left to type.

Fork-Change: F-20
